    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71038.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "The analogy I heard that I think was most appropriate was if a prosecutor had a grand jury indictment and knew that the fix was in at the trial level. They had no responsibility to bring it forward until that situation is rectified in her Lindsey Graham Mitch McConnell say that they are not objective and that they were coordinating with the President of the United States on how it should proceed. Somehow this is like a judge or a jury member or someone else involved in a trial sitting down with the defendant and saying, how would you like us to do this? It's extremely inappropriate. And I think there's at least some basis, some minimum level of what they should do.",
