  {
    "episode_id": 71038,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71038.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "I think people can take any of these things any way they want to and spend it any way they want. I was there the very first day. in intelligence briefings when we were told that the Russians were attacking the electoral process for the upcoming November election. And I've been as active and involved as I'd suggest almost anyone in seeing what took place. So I think our responsibility is to get the facts out there to the American people. The truth has to be known. And if we had not one back to house, people never have found this out. If there wasn't a very courageous whistleblower, people would not have found this out. And for all those who testified, the cream of our diplomatic corps, who spoke truth to power, if they hadn't done that, American people wouldn't know what took place. I think that's the base minimum we owe them. However this plays out, you know, we're not going to get to two thirds, I get that. But for the people who perhaps haven't made up their minds, The small percentage that decide all elections, they need to hear all this. Let's recall, the last election was decided by the electoral vote differences in three states, which Michigan, Wisconsin, and Pennsylvania. That difference was probably about the amount of people who could fit in the soldier field. So we're not trying to shift the president's base. That's not going to happen. But for those folks in the middle who at least ought to be able to make a decision based on the facts of what the president did uh... that's important and and finally let's remember this call to president zalinski took place the day after special counsel molar testify before the american people the president who felt all i got away with it and the next day frankly the only way to describe is he went on to hire crimes and misdemeanors never been held accountable. And unless we at least try to do that, I think he will do, I suspect, higher crimes in misdemeanors, if it's possible.",
