    "turn_text": "So flow was like the first brunch spot I ever went to on the north side. When I moved up here from the south side, I would go there in my twenties. And I get bloody marries with my friends and we share French toast. And still every time I go, I'm like, this place is so good. They have great chiliquilés and huevos rancheros and the best breakfast burrito in town in my opinion. They make three different kinds of bloody marries with different hot sauces. And just great Mexican and Tex-Mex food at night as well. So their brunch is great, but so is the rest of their menu. How long have they been around there? Since 1999. Yeah, it's like a women-owned business and it's a really cool spot and everyone there who works there is great. So",
